    "text_full": "Cookie Settings\nMain Content\nMain Menu\nSEARCH\nMENU\nPeople\nPractices\nInsights\nTrump Administration Resource Center\nON THIS PAGE:\nOverview\nKey Insights\nKey Contacts\nFeatured Content\nOVERVIEW\n\nUnder President Trump’s second term, businesses should prepare for significant policy shifts across industries nationwide—from artificial intelligence and cryptocurrency to telecommunications, renewable energy, and the defense industrial base—bringing both challenges and opportunities that demand agility in navigating an evolving regulatory and enforcement environment.\n\nWiley’s Trump Administration Resource Center provides clients with critical insights and strategic guidance, leveraging our lawyers’ deep understanding of Washington and extensive experience across diverse industries. We are committed to equipping clients with the clarity and foresight needed to adapt to Executive Branch priorities, enabling them to proactively manage compliance, risk, and operational strategies in this rapidly changing legal landscape.\n\nSubscribe to stay connected with our updates and analyses to understand how each development may affect your business in 2025 and beyond.\n\nKey Insights\n\nGovernment Contractors &\nGrantees >\t\nTariffs & Trade Policy >\n\nEmerging Technologies >\t\nOversight, Investigations & White Collar Enforcement >\n\nDEI Counseling >\t\nAdministrative Procedure >\n\n\n\n\n\nKEY CONTACTS\nKey Contacts\n\nElection Law & Government Ethics\n\nMichael E. Toner\nChair\n\n\t\n\nCaleb P. Burns\nPartner\n\n\t\n\nD. Mark Renaud\nPartner\n\n\n\n\nAndrew G. Woodson\nPartner\n\n\t\n\nBrandis L. Zehr\nPartner\n\n\t\n\nRobert L. Walker\nPartner\n\n\n\nEmployment & Labor\n\nOlaoluwaposi O. Oshinowo\nOf Counsel\n\n\t\n\nSavanna L. Shuntich\nSpecial Counsel\n\n\n\nEnvironment & Product Regulation\n\nTracy Heinzman\nChair\n\n\t\n\nJennifer A. Giblin\nPartner\n\n\t\n\nMartha E. Marrapese\nPartner\n\n\t\n\nSara Beth Watson\nOf Counsel\n\n\n\n\nSarah E. Ami